// Build a 0x16-byte data block on the stack.
// Copy ten 16-bit words from RAM starting at 0xFFFFB5A0.
// Read the 16-bit counter at 0xFFFFB5AA and place its
// high and low bytes at buffer offsets 0x12 and 0x13.
// Include additional status data from 0xFFFFB5D9
// and bit 0x10 of 0xFFFFB60E.
// Pass the buffer to sub_5D0D6 with r4 = 0x1FA4.

// Serial communication routine using SCI registers at 0xFFFFF010.
//
// Entry arguments:
//   r4 = 16-bit command/operation value
//   r5 = pointer to data buffer
//   r6 = buffer length in bytes
//
// Saves/configures SCI-related peripheral state through sub_5D79E.
// Performs additional SCI setup through sub_5F116.
// Transmits command-related data, followed by the caller-provided buffer.
// Buffer bytes are read sequentially from r5 for r6 bytes.
// Performs SCI cleanup through sub_5F070 and sub_5D828.
//
// Exact protocol, command encoding, and status-bit meanings
// have not yet been established.
